"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Ordere4d\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nI love Japanese curry, so there is a restaurant near my home that I visit whenever I crave it.  \nTo be honest, I'm not sure if it's traditional Japanese curry, but judging by the ambiance, I can only guess that it resembles homemade curry eaten in Japanese households.  \nIt is run by an international couple—a Japanese wife and a Korean husband—which makes me think it offers an authentic local taste.  \n\nThe interior isn't very large and boiling the noodles seems to take a while, so the food comes out quite slowly; you always have to expect a wait when visiting.  \nEven the slow pace of the food somehow felt charmingly authentic to Japan.  \nFor the waiting list, you go inside to write down your contact information, and when a table opens up, the owner comes outside to call you.  \n\nToday, I headed out early and arrived before opening time, managing to enter right away with an open run.  \nSince the two of them run the place alone, they always look busy—so a pro tip for ordering quickly is to go directly to the counter to place your order.  \n\nI usually have the Gyu-suji Curry Udon and Pollock Roe Soy Milk Cream Udon, but today I specially decided to order the Special Beef and Vegetable Soup Curry Udon.  \nI also picked the Pollock Roe Soy Milk Cream Udon, which I always enjoy.  \n\nAfter placing the order and waiting for more than 20 minutes, the restaurant quickly filled with customers, and a line began forming outside.  \nAfter the long wait, the dishes we ordered finally came out one by one.  \n\nTasting the food, it was indeed that exact curry flavor I always love.  \nThe Special Beef and Vegetable Soup Curry Udon had a slight kick, but it was a gentle heat that wouldn't feel too spicy for Koreans, which was just right.  \nThe Pollock Roe Soy Milk Cream Udon was thick and rich; while the subtle richness of soy milk could feel slightly heavy, the savory, salty pollock roe balanced it cleanly so I could enjoy it harmoniously to the very last bite.  \n\nAs expected, it was another satisfying and delicious meal today.  \nIt was so tasty that I thought I should order extra noodles next time.  \nIf guests ever visit from out of town, this is definitely a restaurant I would love to introduce and invite them to.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n"